; Tutorial_6_Follow_Related_Records.inix -- moving between related tables.

[about]
Title=6 - Follow Related Records
Intro=From a record into the records related to it with Alt plus Right Arrow, and back with Alt plus Left Arrow, as a browser goes back.
Setup=A database with related tables is open; the chinook sample has them.
Homework=Follow a relationship two levels deep, then return with Alt plus Home.

[step]

Say=One want: from an artist, to the albums, to the tracks, and back. Related tables let one record lead to others.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=Shift plus R, R for Related, says what this record leads to, changing nothing.
Key=Shift+R
Hear=(the related tables and their counts)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Right Arrow goes into the related records.
Key=Alt+Right Arrow
Hear=(the child table, and its first record)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus Z says where I am now.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=(the child table, its record count, the filter that ties it to the parent)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Right Arrow again goes a level deeper.
Key=Alt+Right Arrow
Hear=(the next table down)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Left Arrow comes back a level, as a browser goes back.
Key=Alt+Left Arrow
Hear=(the table one level up)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: three levels deep, and lost. Alt plus Home returns to where I started, from any depth.
Key=Alt+Home
Hear=(the starting table, at the record I left)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What ties a record to its relations is its prime, a key DbDo builds from the record itself. Shift plus P, Say Prime, says it.
Key=Shift+P
Hear=Miles Davis
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A related table can have a window of its own. Control plus Shift plus O, Open Table, opens a table in a new window, beside this one.
Key=Control+Shift+O
Hear=Open Table dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose albums and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=albums, 40 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus F4 says the windows open, and Control plus Tab moves between them.
Key=Shift+F4
Hear=2 windows: artists, albums
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=In one window, Control plus F6 moves to the next table, and Alt plus F6 back through the tables visited, as a browser's history does.
Key=Control+F6
Hear=tracks, 412 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F4 closes this window, leaving the first.
Key=Control+F4
Hear=artists, 12 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=F4, Current Windows, lists the windows open, so you can pick one by name rather than cycle through them.
Key=F4
Hear=Current Windows dialog, artists, 1 of 2
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. Alt plus F6 goes back through the tables visited in this window, the way a browser goes back.
Key=Alt+F6
Hear=albums, 40 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus F6 goes forward again.
Key=Alt+Shift+F6
Hear=tracks, 412 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus F4 closes every window but this one, for a clean start.
Key=Control+Shift+F4
Hear=tracks, 412 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Within one window, Control plus Shift plus F6 moves to the previous table, as Control plus F6 moves to the next: Shift reverses.
Key=Control+Shift+F6
Hear=artists, 12 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Whichever way you arrived, Shift plus R still says what this record leads to, so the way down is never a guess.
Key=Shift+R
Hear=albums 3, tracks 31
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Go into related records.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Right Arrow

[step]

Say=Come back a level.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Left Arrow

[step]

Say=Return to the start.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Home
